' ============================================================================
' 39 The tensor value ABI: four Rholang forms and the TL tensors they encode.
'
' Source of Figure TL19 in ../tensor-logic/syntax.md (section 3.3). The
' figure restates the forms V0 to V3 of that section with one example each.
' It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. Each row maps one Rholang value (left) to one TL tensor (right).
'   2. V0 is a number, V1 a rectangular nested list, V2 a relation as a set
'      of tuples of atoms, and V3 a map keyed by atoms.
'   3. The notes give the two rules that keep the encoding unambiguous.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 39-tl-value-abi.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 39-tl-value-abi
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam RectangleBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 60
left to right direction
title The tensor value ABI (forms V0 to V3)

rectangle R3 $rrs_storage [
**V3. Keyed**
an EMap from an atom or a tuple of atoms to V0 or V1
{"Alice": [0.1, 0.9]}
]
rectangle T3 $rrs_tl_engine [
**Mixed dimensions** Sym × Pos(2)
E["Alice", 0] is the double nearest to 0.1,
as an exact dyadic number (floats enter exactly)
]

rectangle R2 $rrs_storage [
**V2. Relation**
an ESet or an EList of ETuples of atoms
Set(("Alice", "Bob"), ("Bob", "Charlie"))
]
rectangle T2 $rrs_tl_engine [
**A Boolean tensor** over Sym × Sym
R("Alice", "Bob") = 1, R("Bob", "Charlie") = 1,
every other pair 0
]

rectangle R1 $rrs_storage [
**V1. Dense**
a rectangular nested EList
[[1, 2], [3, 4]]
]
rectangle T1 $rrs_tl_engine [
**Positional dimensions** Pos(2) × Pos(2)
T[0, 1] = 2, T[1, 0] = 3
]

rectangle R0 $rrs_storage [
**V0. Number**
a number of any kind of decision 54,
for example the GInt 42
]
rectangle T0 $rrs_tl_engine [
**A tensor of rank 0**
the value 42
]

R0 -[$rrs_flow]-> T0
R1 -[$rrs_flow]-> T1
R2 -[$rrs_flow]-> T2
R3 -[$rrs_flow]-> T3

note as RULES
  **Two rules keep the encoding unambiguous**
  A tuple is never a dense element: dense elements are numbers or lists.
  A name in tensors must be a TL identifier and must not shadow a reserved name
  (ReservedName).
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_storage>   | a Rholang value, as it travels in a param or a datum |
|<$rrs_tl_engine> | the tensor that the TL engine decodes |
endlegend
@enduml
